Since "ADHD" is a single condition, it cannot be represented in a JSON format with logical operators. Logical operators are used to combine multiple conditions or criteria, whereas "ADHD" is a single diagnosis.

If you meant to ask for a JSON representation of a study that includes patients with ADHD, here is an example:

"{\n  \"AND\": {\n    \"left\": {\n      \"raw_text\": \"Patients with Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD)\"\n    }\n  }\n}"

This JSON representation simply states that the study includes patients with ADHD. If you need to add additional criteria or conditions, you can modify the JSON structure accordingly.